  <prompt>
    Wire the `participant=` facet on the filtered read endpoint `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=&participant=` (the endpoint + other facets shipped in task 011; `participant=` was stubbed there pending the junction). `participant={personId}` MUST return the messages where that person is a participant in ANY role (From/To/Cc/Bcc), by JOINING the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (task 003 schema, populated by task 050) at MESSAGE grain — returning the `sprk_communication` rows whose junction rows reference the person.

    Requirements (FR-02 completion):
    - Resolve `participant=` against the junction's typed person lookups (`sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact`) — **exact, role-correct, FK-backed matches**, NOT a `sprk_from/to/cc` text-LIKE scan. An unresolved external party is matchable via its `sprk_addresstext` row (`sprk_isresolved=false`).
    - Apply the **SAME impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) access filter** as every other R1 read facet — the `participant=` join MUST NOT bypass `ICommunicationAccessFilter`. No message a caller cannot see may leak because they matched on a participant.
    - Extend the existing read path only: `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `ICommunicationAccessFilter`. Do NOT add a second access mechanism or reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16).
    - `participant=` composes with the other facets (thread/regarding/channel/from/to) as an AND; unknown/empty `participant=` degrades gracefully (no filter).

    Do NOT build the participant WRITE (that is task 050) or a new endpoint (task 011 owns the route).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication read path. Authority on `CommunicationThreadReadService`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, `Access/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs`, and the task-011 filtered `query` endpoint. Fluent in the R1 impersonation + 2-rule access model (the blessed read mechanism — do not fork), ADR-028 (impersonation), ADR-034 (typed person identity), ADR-038 (seam tests as DoD), §10 BFF Hygiene, §11.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `participant={personId}` on the filtered `query` endpoint returns exactly the `sprk_communication` messages where that person participates in any role (From/To/Cc/Bcc), resolved by joining the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction on its typed person lookups (role-exact, FK-backed — not text-LIKE), with unresolved external parties matchable via `sprk_addresstext`. The facet applies the same impersonation + 2-rule access filter as every other read facet (no bypass, no leak) and composes as an AND with the other facets; empty/unknown `participant=` degrades gracefully. Extends the existing read path only (no second access mechanism, no membership-union). Build clean; publish-size delta + CVE + Placement Justification reported; seam tests cover resolved-person, unresolved-address, and a NEGATIVE access case.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Task 011 shipped the filtered `query` endpoint with thread/regarding/channel/from/to reusing the R1 read path; `participant=` was stubbed because no queryable person→communications structure existed. Task 003 adds the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction; task 050 populates it at message grain (one row per message × person/address × role, resolved persons carrying `sprk_systemuser` XOR `sprk_contact`, unresolved external addresses carrying `sprk_addresstext` + `sprk_isresolved=false`). THIS task consumes that index: `participant={personId}` joins the junction and returns the matching messages — the exact, role-precise person filter FR-02 requires (Success Criterion 3: "role-correct rows from the junction, not text-LIKE").

      Component Justification (§11 — modification, not new surface): this task ONLY modifies the existing task-011 query endpoint + read service to add a join clause + reuse the existing access filter — no new endpoint, service, access mechanism, or package. (Per §11, tasks that only modify existing surface do not require the three-question gate; the junction itself was justified in task 003.)

      Access parity (NFR-03, security-relevant): the `participant=` join MUST run under the same impersonation context and the same `ICommunicationAccessFilter` (privacy + internal-only) as the other facets. A person-match MUST NOT surface a message the caller cannot otherwise see. This is the load-bearing correctness property — the negative access case is a required seam test.
    </background>
