  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-02">`participant={personId}` resolves against the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (FR-08) and returns role-exact, FK-backed matches (any of From/To/Cc/Bcc) — NOT a `sprk_from/to/cc` text-LIKE scan. Unresolved external parties matchable via `sprk_addresstext`. Composes as AND with the other facets; empty/unknown degrades gracefully.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03 / ADR-028">Apply the SAME impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) access filter as every other read facet via `ICommunicationAccessFilter`. The participant join MUST NOT bypass the filter — no message a caller cannot see may leak on a participant match.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (access model)">Extend `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `ICommunicationAccessFilter` ONLY. MUST NOT add a second access mechanism or reintroduce membership-union on reads (retired 2026-07-16 — `../messaging-communication-app-r1/notes/access-model-decision.md`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Match on the typed person lookups (`sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact`), consistent with the path-C typed-identity model. MUST NOT reintroduce text-name matching.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Vertical-slice seam tests are the DoD: cover a resolved-person match, an unresolved-address match, the AND-composition with another facet, and a NEGATIVE access case (private/internal-only hidden despite participant match).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline (expected ≈0, no new package); no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` before the PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

