  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the task-011 `query` endpoint + filtered method on `CommunicationThreadReadService`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, `Access/CommunicationAccessFilter.cs`, and the task-003 junction schema + task-050 write shape. Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F. Confirm exactly where the `participant=` stub sits.</step>
    <step order="2">Wire the `participant=` parameter through the endpoint into the filtered query method (compose as AND with thread/regarding/channel/from/to; empty/unknown → no filter).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the junction join: `participant={personId}` selects `sprk_communication` rows that have a `sprk_communicationparticipant` row referencing the person via `sprk_systemuser` or `sprk_contact` (any role). Do NOT text-LIKE `sprk_from/to/cc`.</step>
    <step order="4">Ensure the join runs INSIDE the impersonation + `ICommunicationAccessFilter` path — the participant match MUST NOT bypass the 2-rule filter. Reuse the existing filter; add no second access mechanism; do not reintroduce membership-union.</step>
    <step order="5">Write seam tests (ADR-038): (a) resolved-person `participant={systemuserId}` returns the messages where they are From/To/Cc/Bcc (role-exact, from the junction); (b) an unresolved external party is matchable (via its `sprk_addresstext` row / `isresolved=false`); (c) `participant=` composes as AND with a second facet (e.g. `channel=`); (d) NEGATIVE ACCESS: a private/internal-only message the caller cannot see is NOT returned despite a participant match; (e) empty/unknown `participant=` degrades gracefully (no filter, no error).</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~46.99 MB baseline (expected ≈0).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVE.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: access-filter parity / no bypass, role-exact join not text-LIKE, reuse-not-fork of the read path); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-02, NFR-03, ADR-028, ADR-034, ADR-038). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; read-path edit — coordinate with 050's merge-order since both touch `Services/Communication/`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (051 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (join shape, where the access filter is applied over the join).</step>
  </steps>

